tool.help:
Upload matrix.tsv, variants.tsv and cells.tsv as separate tabular datasets. The matrix has cells in rows and REF/ALT read-count strings in variant columns. Optional selected cells must have one column named cell_barcodes. The tool stages the exact three bundle names and invokes SPICE filter with input_format standard.
The FASTA feeds IUC IQ-TREE 2.4.0. Its supported tree then feeds SPICE Clones. The CSV matrix is the final count-filtered matrix. Selected-cell and variant audit tables describe selection before count filtering; they can include rows later removed. No matrix orientation, IUPAC encoding or filtering order is changed.
@COMMON_HELP@
